DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270206
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270207
SUMMARY:Chinese New Year
DESCRIPTION:Chinese New Year\, also called the Spring Festival\, opens the 
 year in the traditional Chinese lunisolar calendar and runs fifteen days\,
  from the reunion dinner on New Year's Eve to the Lantern Festival. Its da
 te moves: the Congressional Research Service puts the start at the second 
 new moon after the winter solstice\, which falls between January 21 and Fe
 bruary 19. It is not a federal holiday in the United States\, though five 
 states have given it official recognition of some kind.\n\nhttps://todayce
 lebrates.com/holiday/chinese-new-year/
URL;VALUE=URI:https://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/chinese-new-year/
CATEGORIES:Celebration
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CLASS:PUBLIC
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
